course: dictionary
lesson: 10973
title: Warblers: small songbirds
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A warbler is a small bird that sings. Warblers are songbirds, and they are often greenish or brownish, which helps them hide among leaves.
explain: Look at the clues in «a cuckoo leaves its egg for a small reed warbler to raise». The word small tells you the size, and the reed warbler is the bird that raises the cuckoo's chick. Try the swap: put "bird that sings" in place of warbler and see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Warblers eat insects and sing quick, trilling songs. Birdwatchers learn to tell warblers apart by their songs, not just their looks. Warbler can also be an informal word for a person who sings in a wobbly, not very good way.
fact: A warbler is a small songbird, often greenish or brownish, that eats insects.
fact: Warblers sing quick, trilling songs, and birdwatchers learn to tell them apart by their songs.
fact: Many warblers migrate, flying long distances to Britain or North America in spring and leaving in autumn.
fact: «Warble» is the verb: it means to sing with trills and wobbles.
fact: Informally, a warbler can be a person who sings in a wobbly, not very good way.
exercise: What is a warbler in nature lessons? | A fish that lives in rivers | A large bird that cannot sing | A kind of tree | *A small songbird that often eats insects
exercise: Birdwatchers learn to tell warblers apart by what? | Their size only | Their names on signs | Their nests in the snow | *Their songs
exercise: In «a cuckoo leaves its egg for a small reed warbler to raise», which bird raises the cuckoo's egg? | *reed warbler | cuckoo | robin | lyrebird
test: When do many warblers come to Britain or North America? | In winter | Only in the middle of the night | They never come to these places | *In spring
test: Informally, what can a warbler be? | A person who paints pictures | A person who cooks food | A person who runs very fast | *A person who sings in a wobbly, not very good way
exam: «The cuckoo chick's loud begging makes the foster parents feed a chick much bigger than themselves.» What does foster parent mean here? | *A bird that raises a chick that is not its own | A chick that pushes other eggs out | A parent who is a fish | A cuckoo that sings
